WEBVTT

00:00.900 --> 00:03.765
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.196 --> 00:07.460
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.493 --> 00:11.026
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.060 --> 00:14.025
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:14.059 --> 00:17.523
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:17.558 --> 00:20.888
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.923 --> 00:22.421
♪ All the things that make us

00:22.455 --> 00:23.753
♪ Laugh and cry

00:23.787 --> 00:24.861
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.051 --> 00:37.749
We now return to
yet another Indiana Jones movie.

00:38.848 --> 00:41.147
Snakes. Why did it
have to be snakes?

00:41.181 --> 00:42.679
Elderly potheads.

00:42.713 --> 00:45.546
Why did it have to be
elderly potheads?

00:45.580 --> 00:48.111
Is everyone warm in here?
Is it warm?

00:48.145 --> 00:49.544
Brian, are you
feeling all right?

00:49.578 --> 00:51.309
Yeah, I'm fine. It
just seems kind of...

00:52.444 --> 00:53.543
Oh, my God!

00:53.577 --> 00:55.142
Oh, Lois,
your dog threw up.

00:55.176 --> 00:56.907
Peter, Brian's clearly
not feeling well.

00:56.941 --> 00:58.840
You got to take him
to the vet.

00:58.874 --> 01:00.540
Unbelievable!
Brian throws up once,

01:00.574 --> 01:02.339
and you rush him
to the vet.

01:02.373 --> 01:04.338
I was throwing up
all night last night.

01:04.372 --> 01:06.104
Good start.
Keep it up, snack pack.

01:08.571 --> 01:10.369
Peter, you got
to take him now!

01:10.404 --> 01:12.201
L-Lois, it's probably
just something I ate.

01:12.236 --> 01:13.501
I-I'm fine.
Really.

01:13.536 --> 01:16.534
I-I got more energy than
a cruise ship conga line.

01:16.568 --> 01:18.365
♪ Horny on a big boat

01:18.400 --> 01:20.165
♪ Horny
on a big boat! ♪

01:20.199 --> 01:22.831
I'm very sick
from lobster.

01:27.398 --> 01:29.329
Brian, your blood work
shows that your liver

01:29.363 --> 01:30.494
isn't functioning
properly.

01:30.529 --> 01:32.293
Would you happen
to be a drinker?

01:32.328 --> 01:34.693
Well, I don't know
if I'd label myself a drinker.

01:34.728 --> 01:37.859
I know I like a cold beer
after I mow the lawn.

01:37.894 --> 01:40.057
There were three lies
in that sentence.

01:40.091 --> 01:42.357
Brian, have you ever heard
of Lou Gehrig's disease?

01:42.392 --> 01:43.423
Oh, no!

01:43.457 --> 01:45.823
Well, you have
Mickey Mantle's disease.

01:45.857 --> 01:49.687
Now, the most obvious step would
simply be to stop drinking.

01:49.722 --> 01:50.953
Or...?

01:50.988 --> 01:53.153
Well, we do have these pills
that may correct

01:53.187 --> 01:55.385
the enzyme imbalance in your liver.
Yeah, that one.

01:55.419 --> 01:56.852
Okay, I'll be
in the waiting room

01:56.887 --> 01:58.684
barking at the fish
in the tank.

01:58.719 --> 01:59.851
All right,
Mr. Griffin,

01:59.886 --> 02:01.717
these pills will clear up
Brian's condition.

02:01.751 --> 02:04.915
But unfortunately, they only
come in suppository form.

02:04.949 --> 02:05.947
Uh...

02:05.948 --> 02:07.747
It means they have
to be inserted

02:07.781 --> 02:09.113
into the patient's anus.

02:09.147 --> 02:11.880
Oh, you're a
dirty doctor, aren't you?

02:11.914 --> 02:14.378
Mr. Griffin, I'm not joking--
or a doctor.

02:14.412 --> 02:16.410
Now, you'll need
to administer these pills,

02:16.444 --> 02:19.210
because no dog ever voluntarily
takes a suppository.

02:19.244 --> 02:20.841
Well, one in ten does.

02:20.876 --> 02:23.141
Oh, I know the one--
Brian's cousin Jasper.

02:23.175 --> 02:24.773
His bum looks
like that guy

02:24.808 --> 02:26.974
with a hundred cigarettes
in his mouth.

02:35.270 --> 02:37.436
Hey, Chris, I noticed
you were sitting alone.

02:37.471 --> 02:38.968
You mind if I join you?

02:39.002 --> 02:40.602
Sure. We both
have hats.

02:40.636 --> 02:42.601
Makes sense.
Oh, thanks.

02:42.634 --> 02:45.232
Hey, can you check my back
for "kick me" signs?

02:45.266 --> 02:47.432
Oh, yeah, you got
a couple.

02:47.467 --> 02:49.564
This one says you're
a "dirty kick."

02:49.599 --> 02:51.564
That doesn't say "kick,"
but thanks,

02:51.599 --> 02:53.797
I'll keep that one
for my lawsuit.

02:53.831 --> 02:55.928
Boys, I got a
new home gym.

02:55.963 --> 02:57.927
Why are you telling us that?

02:57.962 --> 02:59.594
Just letting
people know.

02:59.628 --> 03:03.126
Don't want anyone to get freaked
out by the transformation.

03:03.160 --> 03:05.157
I got to say, it
feels kind of weird

03:05.192 --> 03:06.859
having someone
join me for lunch.

03:06.893 --> 03:08.290
Well, it's
only natural, Chris.

03:08.324 --> 03:10.290
You and I are
social exiles.

03:10.324 --> 03:13.089
We're the Khaleesi and
Jorah Mormont of this school.

03:13.123 --> 03:15.588
Sure, I'll agree to keep
the conversation going.

03:15.622 --> 03:18.854
Well, time to break out
my terrible Jewish bag lunch.

03:18.888 --> 03:20.453
Let's see.
Smoked whitefish,

03:20.488 --> 03:22.452
herring in cream sauce,
smoked sable--

03:22.487 --> 03:24.118
that's a different kind
of whitefish--

03:24.152 --> 03:27.049
and for dessert, the only
bad cookie in the world.

03:27.084 --> 03:29.215
<i>Hey, what's it like
buying food from school?</i>

03:29.249 --> 03:31.315
It's good. I know
everyone back there,

03:31.350 --> 03:33.347
so they let me drink
their corn water.

03:33.381 --> 03:36.113
Boy, it's so great having
someone I can talk to.

03:36.147 --> 03:37.613
I feel the same way, Chris.

03:37.647 --> 03:40.112
I think you and I could
get along very nicely.

03:40.146 --> 03:43.778
Yeah. We'll be a better team
than the Warsaw Globetrotters.

03:43.812 --> 03:45.309
♪ Dribble, dribble, dribble

03:45.344 --> 03:46.676
♪ Tuck in shirt

03:46.710 --> 03:48.875
♪ Give to my friend

03:48.909 --> 03:50.407
♪ Spin on finger

03:50.442 --> 03:51.841
♪ Two rotations

03:51.875 --> 03:54.073
♪ Dream about window

03:54.107 --> 03:56.605
♪ Put away basketball,
go to work ♪

03:56.639 --> 03:59.804
♪ In calcium mine.

04:03.803 --> 04:05.835
All right, Brian,
it's time for you to take

04:05.869 --> 04:07.468
one of these pills
from the vet.

04:07.502 --> 04:09.633
Oh, yeah, right. Can we
do what we normally do,

04:09.668 --> 04:11.466
where you roll it up
in a piece of cheese

04:11.500 --> 04:13.066
like you're fooling me?
Yeah, I guess,

04:13.100 --> 04:15.131
but then you're gonna
have cheese in your ass.

04:15.167 --> 04:16.698
W-Wait, what?
Yeah, the doctor said

04:16.732 --> 04:18.932
I got to give you
these pills the butt way.

04:18.965 --> 04:20.763
Oh, no, no, no, no.
That is not happening.

04:20.797 --> 04:22.762
No, no, no. I do not
go the butt way.

04:22.796 --> 04:24.361
Look, I know it sounds
a little rough,

04:24.395 --> 04:26.861
but why don't we start with
a gentle massage of the area

04:26.895 --> 04:28.026
and see how you feel?

04:28.061 --> 04:29.460
Peter, get away from my ass!

04:29.494 --> 04:31.992
Br-Brian! No!

04:32.026 --> 04:34.858
Huh. Guess I'm just gonna
have to take him by surprise.

04:34.892 --> 04:36.290
Shouldn't be too hard.

04:36.325 --> 04:38.689
After all, I used to be
a Pete-in-the-box.

04:51.018 --> 04:53.151
Goes the weasel!

04:56.317 --> 04:58.248
All right, if I'm gonna
give Brian his medicine,

04:58.282 --> 05:00.247
<i>I should probably watch
that old episode of Lassie</i>

05:00.281 --> 05:02.847
where Timmy has to give
her a suppository.

05:06.547 --> 05:08.745
What's that, Lassie?
You feel sick?

05:08.779 --> 05:11.376
What's wrong, girl?

05:12.710 --> 05:14.008
A supposi-what?

05:14.043 --> 05:16.274
What am I supposed
to do with it?

05:17.543 --> 05:19.007
Gosh. I...

05:19.041 --> 05:22.406
Well, if you're
in that much pain, I-I guess.

05:22.441 --> 05:24.005
Okay.

05:29.504 --> 05:30.636
You were lying?

05:30.670 --> 05:32.069
<i>You weren't
feeling sick?</i>

05:32.103 --> 05:33.501
I don't understand.

05:33.536 --> 05:35.600
Why did you want me
to do this?

05:37.267 --> 05:39.232
What?!
He was in on it?

05:39.266 --> 05:40.900
It was just a prank?

05:40.933 --> 05:42.965
You guys are gross!

05:46.931 --> 05:49.061
Kids, everybody, family meeting!

05:49.095 --> 05:51.128
There's too much passing
gas in this house.

05:51.162 --> 05:53.560
So from now on, anytime
you got to cut one,

05:53.594 --> 05:55.760
you pull your pants
down and you do it

05:55.795 --> 05:56.926
through this
fart hole.

05:56.960 --> 05:58.226
Are you insane?

05:58.260 --> 05:59.825
Lois, it's
okay-- it's all a trick.

05:59.859 --> 06:02.424
As soon as Brian does it, I'm
gonna be on the other side,

06:02.458 --> 06:03.989
and I'll stick
the suppository in.

06:04.024 --> 06:05.589
No. Absolutely not.

06:05.624 --> 06:07.588
I am not living like this.

06:07.623 --> 06:10.986
You think Morgan Fairchild
has a fart hole in her house?

06:11.021 --> 06:13.387
Morgan, the coq
Au vin is divine.

06:13.422 --> 06:15.052
But so rich.

06:15.086 --> 06:17.085
Will you excuse me?

06:21.183 --> 06:23.283
Where do our
Hollywood farts go?

06:23.317 --> 06:26.915
I've heard they're filtered
into Tom Sizemore's house.

06:30.114 --> 06:32.912
Ah... Morgan.

06:37.011 --> 06:38.643
Hey, no, no.
No, no, Brian.

06:38.677 --> 06:40.675
No, no. You win.
You win. I quit.

06:40.710 --> 06:42.675
It's your liver; you
do whatever you want.

06:42.710 --> 06:44.608
Well, thank you.
Yes, it is my liver,

06:44.642 --> 06:46.541
and I don't want
to take that pill.

06:46.575 --> 06:48.139
Fine. We're both
in agreement.

06:48.173 --> 06:49.906
So let's just
both watch TV.

06:49.940 --> 06:52.038
And nothing else.
Sounds good to me.

06:52.072 --> 06:54.270
I'm glad you think
it sounds good.

06:56.371 --> 06:57.669
It's nice to watch TV

06:57.704 --> 06:59.702
when you have nothing
else to do, isn't it?

06:59.735 --> 07:00.902
Yeah.

07:00.936 --> 07:02.667
Get over here, you idiot!
Peter! What the hell?

07:02.702 --> 07:04.504
I'm still in charge of you!
Stop it! Get away from me!

07:04.505 --> 07:05.166
I'm a human!

07:05.167 --> 07:07.065
This is for your benefit,
so just go limp and take it!

07:07.100 --> 07:08.866
You touch my ass,
I swear to God I'll kill you!

07:13.597 --> 07:15.363
Wha... What the hell?

07:15.397 --> 07:17.528
You... you bit me!

07:17.562 --> 07:19.261
You're damn right I did!
And I'll do it again

07:19.295 --> 07:21.026
if you don't stay
the hell away from my ass!

07:21.060 --> 07:22.926
But, Brian, the vet said...

07:24.260 --> 07:26.458
Wow, where did that come from?

07:26.493 --> 07:27.890
God, that was so intense.

07:27.924 --> 07:30.790
I feel more powerful
than a lesbian's crotch.

07:32.056 --> 07:34.555
Ooh, sorry, ma'am,
we don't valet motorcycles.

07:34.590 --> 07:36.422
Heh. Don't need to.

07:46.385 --> 07:48.016
Lois, can you pour
my juice?

07:48.050 --> 07:49.416
I can't lift my arm.

07:49.450 --> 07:51.383
I still can't believe
Brian bit you.

07:51.417 --> 07:53.214
It just doesn't
seem like him.

07:53.249 --> 07:55.214
Oh, yeah, 'cause you
know him so well.

07:55.249 --> 07:56.747
Shut your face.

07:59.547 --> 08:01.677
Oh. Uh... hey, Brian.

08:02.912 --> 08:05.377
Get out of that chair.
Leave the eggs.

08:05.411 --> 08:07.409
But this is my breakfast.

08:14.108 --> 08:16.674
Honey, when did Peter Griffin
take up jogging?

08:16.707 --> 08:18.671
I don't know, dear.
By the way,

08:18.705 --> 08:21.371
we're the couple who lives
a few blocks away.

08:27.663 --> 08:30.061
We now return
to an '80s teen movie

08:30.095 --> 08:31.827
at a realistic high school.

08:31.861 --> 08:33.893
You're going down at
that karate tournament.

08:33.927 --> 08:35.393
I don't think so.

08:35.427 --> 08:36.824
You guys do karate?

08:36.858 --> 08:38.924
You're both
losers.

08:38.958 --> 08:41.423
Uh, morning, sir.

08:41.457 --> 08:43.588
So, Peter, I assume if
you're watching TV,

08:43.623 --> 08:45.821
that means you already
did all my chores?

08:45.855 --> 08:47.255
I-I sure did, sure did.

08:47.289 --> 08:49.453
I scared off the mailman,
threatened Quagmire's cat,

08:49.488 --> 08:51.487
and I even took
your bath for you.

08:51.521 --> 08:53.684
Now I'm just gonna reach
for the shampoo.

08:53.719 --> 08:55.484
No jumping out.

08:59.517 --> 09:01.083
He's got Rupert!

09:01.117 --> 09:02.548
Hey, drop it.
Drop it.

09:02.582 --> 09:04.115
Drop it.

09:04.149 --> 09:06.114
All right, I need you to
buy a birthday present

09:06.148 --> 09:08.913
for my friend Jeff-- he likes
the Packers and surfing.

09:08.947 --> 09:10.345
Enough is enough, Peter.

09:10.380 --> 09:12.677
The dog's not in charge
of this house.

09:12.712 --> 09:15.610
First thing tomorrow, I'm
taking Brian to obedience school

09:15.644 --> 09:17.842
so we can get him
back under control.

09:17.877 --> 09:20.409
You know, sending him to school
wouldn't be the worst idea.

09:20.443 --> 09:23.773
He might even enjoy it.
I know I had a blast in college.

09:23.808 --> 09:26.639
Man, I love college.
So many chicks, so many parties.

09:26.673 --> 09:28.205
Yeah, totally.

09:28.239 --> 09:30.238
I'm supposed to meet
the R.A. for coffee

09:30.272 --> 09:31.970
later in the common room,
but until then,

09:32.005 --> 09:33.903
I'm just gonna walk around
with my shower caddy

09:33.937 --> 09:36.767
and see what people wrote
on their whiteboards.

09:40.701 --> 09:44.032
Uh, before I touch anything,
is this a nut-free counter?

09:44.066 --> 09:47.430
I don't know-- my dad's might
have been on there this morning.

09:47.465 --> 09:48.797
Oh, hey, Meg.

09:48.831 --> 09:52.030
I saw you stomp that pigeon
today with your bare foot.

09:52.064 --> 09:53.728
Pretty powerful stuff.

09:53.762 --> 09:56.495
Thanks. I don't like losing
any part of my lunch.

09:56.529 --> 09:59.027
Look, I'd love to stay and talk,
Neil, but I have homework,

09:59.062 --> 10:01.158
and there was no toilet paper
in the girls' bathroom.

10:01.193 --> 10:03.558
Well, while you freshen up,
maybe I could help you get

10:03.593 --> 10:04.957
a head start
on that homework.

10:04.992 --> 10:06.124
You'd do that?

10:06.158 --> 10:07.857
Wow, that'd be great!

10:07.891 --> 10:11.156
Wait, Neil, I thought you and I
were gonna go find unlocked cars

10:11.190 --> 10:12.888
and pretend
we're driving them.

10:12.922 --> 10:15.954
Sorry, Chris.
Booty calls.

10:15.989 --> 10:17.354
What was that all about?

10:17.388 --> 10:19.885
Well, I guess
I have to do it by myself.

10:21.852 --> 10:24.684
Boy, this light
is taking forever!

10:25.684 --> 10:28.016
Please get out.
I never drive this car.

10:28.050 --> 10:29.982
My wife died in it.

10:35.913 --> 10:38.378
Listen up, maggots,
you're in my house now!

10:38.412 --> 10:40.178
There are no belly
scratches here!

10:40.212 --> 10:41.876
There are no table scraps!

10:41.910 --> 10:43.543
What we have here are good dogs!

10:43.578 --> 10:46.009
No bandana-wearing,
Frisbee-catching hippie dogs!

10:46.043 --> 10:49.141
No parking lot, hind-leg dancing
YouTube dogs!

10:49.176 --> 10:52.440
No crime solving, camera
mugging Scooby Dooby dogs!

10:52.473 --> 10:53.838
Oh, no Scooby Doo, huh?

10:53.872 --> 10:55.305
Ruh-roh.

10:55.340 --> 10:57.470
Oh, it seems we got
us a comedy dog.

10:57.504 --> 10:59.937
Are you Kathy Griffin?
'Cause I ain't laughing.

10:59.971 --> 11:01.437
So maybe you are
Kathy Griffin.

11:01.471 --> 11:03.003
Or maybe you're
that comedy dog

11:03.037 --> 11:05.102
with Robert Smigel's
hand up your backside.

11:05.136 --> 11:07.134
Well, let me tell you
something, comedy dog.

11:07.169 --> 11:08.866
<i>You're here for
me to poop on!</i>

11:08.900 --> 11:10.731
All right, first of all,
it seems like

11:10.766 --> 11:13.298
you have a lot of opinions
about a lot of comedians.

11:13.333 --> 11:14.530
And second of all... Ow!

11:14.565 --> 11:16.397
That hurts!
- That's right.

11:16.432 --> 11:18.496
<i>Silent and terrible,
like The Artist.</i>

11:18.530 --> 11:20.463
I watch a lot of
TV and movies.

11:20.497 --> 11:22.794
I am your media-savvy
worst nightmare!

11:22.829 --> 11:25.493
Now, down on all fours
like the rest of them!

11:25.527 --> 11:28.192
That's right, we got ways
to break your spirit!

11:28.226 --> 11:32.757
In fact, you seem like a
prime candidate for The Chair.

11:44.820 --> 11:47.551
Honey, did you hear
a dog scream?

11:47.585 --> 11:49.551
Yes, I did, dear.

11:49.585 --> 11:52.583
Our summer cabin is near
the obedience school.

11:56.716 --> 11:58.780
Move along.
Got to keep the hallway clear.

11:58.815 --> 12:00.746
This isn't because
of my divorce.

12:00.780 --> 12:02.179
Good for him.

12:02.213 --> 12:04.878
He actually followed through.

12:06.578 --> 12:08.677
What the hell? Again?

12:08.711 --> 12:10.376
Thanks for doing
my book report, Neil.

12:10.411 --> 12:12.542
And I didn't even have
to change the handwriting,

12:12.576 --> 12:14.075
'cause you write
like a girl.

12:14.109 --> 12:16.007
You should see me throw.

12:16.042 --> 12:18.673
Listen, Meg, would you want
to go to a movie sometime?

12:18.707 --> 12:20.704
You know what?

12:20.739 --> 12:22.704
I'd like that.
It's a date.

12:22.739 --> 12:24.837
Okay, well, I'll, uh...
I'll see you later.

12:24.871 --> 12:26.737
Home Ec just got out.

12:26.771 --> 12:28.769
I'm gonna go lick
all their bowls.

12:30.004 --> 12:32.567
Hey, Neil.
Oh, h-hey, Chris.

12:32.601 --> 12:35.698
You sure are spending a lot
of time with my sister lately.

12:35.733 --> 12:37.565
You know, if I didn't
know better,

12:37.599 --> 12:39.597
I'd think
that fish are ghosts.

12:39.632 --> 12:42.531
And I'd also think
you're putting the moves on Meg.

12:44.098 --> 12:47.195
Listen, Chris, you're my
friend, so I have to confess.

12:47.230 --> 12:49.429
My sitting with you
at lunch was part

12:49.462 --> 12:52.327
of a carefully laid-out plan
to get close to your sister.

12:52.361 --> 12:54.259
What?!
Look, I know it sounds terrible.

12:54.294 --> 12:57.358
But-but still, we've had
some good times together.

12:57.393 --> 13:00.257
We even got Sean Penn
to dress up as my dad.

13:02.791 --> 13:05.555
Go away! I never want
to talk to you again!

13:06.955 --> 13:08.520
God, I should have known it.

13:08.554 --> 13:09.987
I feel more betrayed

13:10.022 --> 13:12.818
than when I thought
that lawyer was gonna propose.

13:12.852 --> 13:14.584
So you did
commit the murder?

13:14.619 --> 13:16.151
Uh-huh.

13:16.185 --> 13:18.517
And you admit it here
in front of everyone?

13:18.551 --> 13:20.083
Uh-huh.

13:20.117 --> 13:22.416
No further questions,
Your Honor.

13:22.450 --> 13:24.747
Wait. No further questions?

13:24.782 --> 13:28.746
Motion to have the last eight
years stricken from the record!

13:36.844 --> 13:38.409
Hey, Brian,
you're back!

13:38.443 --> 13:40.575
Come on in.
In... inside?

13:40.610 --> 13:42.508
Are-are...
are you sure?

13:42.542 --> 13:44.140
Yeah, what-what...
yeah, what do you think,

13:44.174 --> 13:46.040
I'm gonna make you
stay in the yard?

13:46.074 --> 13:48.072
Get in here.

13:49.639 --> 13:53.570
Sir, if it takes the rest of
my life, I will repay you.

13:53.605 --> 13:54.904
Who's this puss?

13:54.938 --> 13:56.769
Oh, no, no, no,
I'm-I'm not a cat.

13:56.803 --> 13:58.834
I'm-I'm a dog.
I'm your pet.

13:58.869 --> 14:01.001
And-and I'm just happy
to be here.

14:01.035 --> 14:03.066
Brian, what did they do
to you at that school?

14:03.101 --> 14:05.165
You're-you're
so... submissive.

14:05.200 --> 14:07.498
Yes, looks like someone's
gone at him with a "hwhip."

14:07.532 --> 14:10.330
That is... that is a perfectly
valid way of saying that.

14:10.365 --> 14:12.330
Bravo, Master.
Master?

14:12.365 --> 14:16.095
And a surprisingly quick
erection for Stewie.

14:22.651 --> 14:24.616
There you go.

14:24.650 --> 14:25.825
You-you look
very dapper, sir.

14:25.826 --> 14:27.058
Thanks, Brian.

14:27.093 --> 14:28.658
God, I love the new you.

14:28.692 --> 14:30.890
That obedience school really
schooled you in obedience.

14:32.190 --> 14:33.856
That's why it's
called that!

14:33.890 --> 14:36.721
Permission to take fast,
tiny bites of my own tail, sir?

14:36.755 --> 14:38.754
Granted.

14:38.788 --> 14:40.453
You're wearing a bow tie?

14:40.488 --> 14:41.886
What's the occasion?

14:41.921 --> 14:43.120
No occasion, Lois.

14:43.154 --> 14:45.120
I just want to piss
a couple of guys off.

14:45.154 --> 14:46.618
What the hell are you doing?

14:46.652 --> 14:48.351
You think you're
better than us?

14:48.385 --> 14:50.682
No way you tied
that on your own.

14:55.181 --> 14:56.714
I'm glad we got here early.

14:56.748 --> 14:58.147
I like to watch
the previews.

14:58.181 --> 15:01.579
Yeah, and also the friendly
warning about theater shootings.

15:02.946 --> 15:05.677
♪ Don't get shot by a bullet

15:05.712 --> 15:08.176
♪ Don't get shot
by a bullet ♪

15:08.211 --> 15:11.175
♪ Keep your wits about you

15:11.210 --> 15:14.141
♪ This place used to be fun!

15:14.175 --> 15:15.906
You know, this is nice.

15:15.940 --> 15:18.039
It's actually the first time
I've been on a date

15:18.074 --> 15:19.605
since I got the nickname
Gutterball.

15:19.639 --> 15:20.971
It is nice.

15:21.006 --> 15:22.572
Here, hold still.

15:23.604 --> 15:25.603
Make a wish.

15:26.603 --> 15:28.502
What did you wish for?

15:28.536 --> 15:29.901
This.

15:32.968 --> 15:36.333
You used me just so
you could date my sister!

15:36.367 --> 15:38.299
Oh, my God! Chris?!

15:38.333 --> 15:39.631
I'm so sorry!

15:39.665 --> 15:41.430
Oh, what have I done?!

15:41.465 --> 15:43.496
Aw, crap.

15:43.530 --> 15:45.129
Okay, Dad, you got us in.

15:45.163 --> 15:46.962
Now just go.

15:51.794 --> 15:53.758
Cleveland,
what are you looking at?

15:53.793 --> 15:55.126
I'm on edge.

15:55.160 --> 15:57.091
<i>Saw Halloween II
last night.</i>

15:57.124 --> 15:58.257
Brian, go outside.

15:58.292 --> 15:59.755
Keep guard
for Michael Myers.

15:59.790 --> 16:01.922
If he seem like he
dead, he ain't dead!

16:01.957 --> 16:03.322
Boy, Peter, seems like

16:03.356 --> 16:05.155
that obedience school
did wonders for Brian.

16:05.190 --> 16:06.554
Oh, yeah, it's great.

16:06.588 --> 16:08.519
He'll do anything
I tell him to now.

16:08.555 --> 16:10.019
Maybe I should
send Bonnie.

16:14.817 --> 16:16.749
Oh. Oh, my!

16:19.049 --> 16:20.715
All right, somebody
say something else.

16:20.749 --> 16:23.481
No. You need to know
what you did.

16:27.448 --> 16:28.679
Hey, Brian, you know...

16:28.713 --> 16:30.045
you know what we should do?

16:30.080 --> 16:32.277
Let's you and me go pee
in Meg's bed.

16:32.311 --> 16:34.076
That's-that's always fun.

16:34.110 --> 16:35.409
Pee in her bed?

16:35.444 --> 16:37.275
I-I... I could never do that.

16:37.309 --> 16:39.241
That-that... that'd be
peeing in the house,

16:39.276 --> 16:40.740
and that's-that's...
that's bad dog stuff.

16:40.775 --> 16:42.441
That-that's not good dog stuff!

16:42.475 --> 16:44.606
Wait. What?
What are you talking about?

16:44.640 --> 16:47.073
Forgive me for speaking
out of turn, sir,

16:47.107 --> 16:49.538
but you sent me to that
school to change me.

16:49.572 --> 16:51.270
It was your turn,
wasn't it?

16:51.304 --> 16:53.270
First, I went,
and you went?

16:53.304 --> 16:54.935
We best get you
to bed, sir.

16:54.969 --> 16:56.734
Oh, come on, Brian.
It's still early.

16:56.769 --> 16:58.934
Let's just... let's go throw
potatoes at Cleveland's house.

16:58.968 --> 17:00.034
You go ahead.

17:00.069 --> 17:01.799
I've got to go make
the waffle fries

17:01.833 --> 17:04.466
that you scream-requested
in the car.

17:04.500 --> 17:06.796
Geez, what the hell
happened to him?

17:06.830 --> 17:10.429
We used to be so close,
but now we seem so different.

17:10.463 --> 17:11.695
Like a whale

17:11.729 --> 17:14.628
and his developmentally-disabled
brother.

17:18.528 --> 17:20.093
Hi, guys!

17:21.326 --> 17:24.690
Get in my mouth,
you hundreds of fish.

17:28.223 --> 17:31.820
A record crowd
of 65 people turned out

17:31.855 --> 17:33.587
for Free Jerky Stick Night.

17:33.621 --> 17:35.686
Hey, that sounds
pretty good to me.

17:35.720 --> 17:37.686
Traffic on 146 is backed up
all the way

17:37.720 --> 17:38.685
to Mineral Spring Avenue...

17:38.719 --> 17:40.684
What do you want, Neil?

17:40.718 --> 17:42.550
And why are you
playing the news?

17:42.584 --> 17:43.917
Oh, it's an old boom box.

17:43.951 --> 17:45.216
I don't own any cassettes,

17:45.251 --> 17:47.549
so I just have to play
whatever's on the radio.

17:47.583 --> 17:49.614
Shouldn't you be out with Meg?

17:49.649 --> 17:52.247
Look, Chris,
I-I'm sorry I lied to you,

17:52.281 --> 17:55.113
but I'd still like
to be friends, and I hope...

17:55.148 --> 17:57.444
I'm sorry.
I have to put the boom box down.

17:57.478 --> 17:59.377
The D batteries
make it very heavy.

17:59.412 --> 18:00.809
Neil! There you are!

18:00.844 --> 18:02.510
What the hell
is your problem?!

18:02.545 --> 18:04.043
I finally give
you a shot,

18:04.077 --> 18:06.208
and you abandon me
in a movie theater?!

18:13.804 --> 18:15.304
I'm sorry, Meg,

18:15.339 --> 18:17.903
but my friendship
with Chris is more important.

18:17.937 --> 18:20.469
You're a jerk, Neil!

18:20.504 --> 18:22.102
So what do you say, Chris?

18:22.137 --> 18:23.600
Can we hang out again?

18:23.635 --> 18:26.534
Yeah. I'd like that, Neil.

18:26.568 --> 18:28.766
Great. See you tomorrow.

18:37.031 --> 18:39.096
This is 'cause I'm drunk!

18:39.131 --> 18:41.395
Move out, Irish trash!

18:46.693 --> 18:49.125
Hey, Lois, you noticed
ever since Brian came back

18:49.158 --> 18:51.491
from obedience school
that things have been weird?

18:51.525 --> 18:53.023
What do you mean?

18:53.057 --> 18:54.922
Well, he just lets me
order him around,

18:54.956 --> 18:57.555
and he-he never wants to do
fun stuff together like before.

18:57.589 --> 18:59.887
I mean, the thing I always
loved about Brian was

18:59.921 --> 19:01.953
that he wasn't just a pet.

19:01.988 --> 19:03.120
He was a friend.

19:03.154 --> 19:05.418
And I miss that friend.

19:05.452 --> 19:08.617
I think we just have to accept
that this is how he is now.

19:08.651 --> 19:10.417
Don't forget,
he bit you, Peter.

19:10.450 --> 19:12.250
I mean, what if he bit Stewie?

19:12.284 --> 19:14.082
How about
you bite me, bitch?

19:14.117 --> 19:15.681
Wait a minute. You're right!

19:15.716 --> 19:17.547
He bit me!

19:17.581 --> 19:19.547
I know what I got to do.

19:20.714 --> 19:22.578
I'm sorry.
Was that too harsh?

19:22.613 --> 19:24.843
It sounded more
playful in my head.

19:31.942 --> 19:33.308
I'm sorry, Brian,

19:33.342 --> 19:35.907
but I'm doing this in
the name of friendship.

19:41.139 --> 19:43.437
Ah, damn it!
What the hell, Peter?!

19:43.472 --> 19:45.470
Oh, my God.

19:45.504 --> 19:47.103
Oh, my God, I bit you!

19:47.137 --> 19:48.370
I'm-I'm so sorry, sir!

19:48.404 --> 19:50.202
No, no, no, it's
okay! It's okay!

19:50.236 --> 19:51.534
Don't you see, Brian?

19:51.568 --> 19:52.868
That's the
appropriate response

19:52.902 --> 19:54.533
if anyone gets
near your anus.

19:54.567 --> 19:57.132
Look, we were wrong
to try to change you.

19:57.166 --> 19:59.031
I-I just want
the old you back.

19:59.066 --> 20:00.365
You do?

20:00.399 --> 20:02.363
But-but I was a bad dog.

20:02.397 --> 20:04.928
I know, but that's what I
liked about you, you know?

20:04.963 --> 20:07.495
You were fun, we got into
trouble together, we got...

20:07.529 --> 20:09.893
Uh-oh. Uh-oh. I just rubbed
my eye with this finger.

20:09.927 --> 20:11.627
Am I gonna be okay?
Am I gonna be okay?

20:11.661 --> 20:12.859
Wait, how do
you get pinkeye?

20:12.893 --> 20:14.492
Oh, God, this has
got to be it.

20:14.526 --> 20:18.024
Peter, I want things back
the way they were, too.

20:18.058 --> 20:19.423
That's what I want!

20:19.458 --> 20:21.690
Look, I'm really sorry
I bit you.

20:21.724 --> 20:22.922
Oh, forget all that.

20:22.957 --> 20:25.521
I'm just happy
to have my best friend back.

20:25.555 --> 20:27.753
I missed you, Brian.

20:27.788 --> 20:31.318
I've missed you, too, Peter.

20:31.353 --> 20:33.318
Welcome back, buddy.

20:33.353 --> 20:39.845
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru

20:42.049 --> 20:44.848
And now I'm gonna go upstairs
and pee in Meg's bed.

20:44.882 --> 20:46.080
No.

20:46.114 --> 20:48.245
<i>We're gonna go pee
in Meg's bed.</i>

20:48.280 --> 20:50.578
Good boy.

20:50.612 --> 20:52.044
Hey, what's up?

20:52.079 --> 20:54.477
I didn't know we could do finger
stuff in the public rooms.